message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "HASH$CyberAxe: HASH$CyberAxe research toolkit source collection"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Jeremy
    family-names: Benisek
    alias: CyberAxe
    website: "https://cyberaxe.dev/"
url: "https://hashcyberaxe.com/"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jbenisek/hash-cyberaxe-toolkit-source"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
date-released: "2026-11-06"
abstract: "The full source of the HASH$CyberAxe research tools: the programs and scripts used to study reduced-round SHA-256, BLAKE3, SHA-3 and Poseidon. It covers characteristic builders, SAT encoders, independent verifiers, schedule diagnostics, BLAKE3 circuit kernels, cost calculators and the browser labs. Use it to see how a published result was produced, run a method on your own inputs, or build a new tool from the same parts. There are 19 tool families; each has a README in readmes/ and setup guides in guides/."
keywords:
  - cryptanalysis
  - SHA-256
  - BLAKE3
  - SHA-3
  - Poseidon
  - reproducibility
